Z||000022||Coconut||02-16-2001||03:22 PM||||Made it in to work this morning at 5:30 <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>On the way over, saw a couple of cars parked in the ditch <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Can't figure out why some of these people can't exercise a little common sense when it comes to the slippery stuff. It really wasn't that bad, I guess they were in too much of a hurry. I'll hafta admit, for a fleeting moment, I thought about calling in today but I quickly came to my senses in light of losing a day on wednesday due to a stupid dynamite scare about a block away from where I work. Local authorities shut down all buisnesses and even the freeway (I-5) that were close to the site.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Cruisin' (all bundled up and toasty)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||12
Z||000023||onfire||02-18-2001||03:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B>A week or two? I wish, but I don't think so. Just out of curiosity, how long have you lived in the area? Enjoy it while it's here!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ya, wishful thinking. I should have said a day or two. I justed get a little excited when I see snow. Gonna have to go up to the mountains and play in the snow. I just came back from Spokane Saturday, they don't have much snow left either. I have lived here for about 21 yrs or so.||||reg||1
